{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     training/sections — the tracks grid. "Inside the stages."
     Ported from NS-Design-System/preview/demo-training-index.html §03.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ HARDCODED, ON PURPOSE AND ON REQUEST. These are SECTIONS of the
     curriculum as an editorial map — the shape the training is planned to
     take — not a list of what is published. That is why they are copy and why
     they can name tracks that have no posts behind them yet.

     It is the band directly above training/modules, and the pair is the whole
     argument of the page:

       sections  what the curriculum WILL cover   ← this file, copy
       modules   what is written TODAY            ← Ghost, never copy

     Keeping them adjacent is what stops the page overclaiming: a reader sees
     the plan and then immediately sees how much of it exists.

     ⚠ PEERS, NOT A SEQUENCE. .ns-grid with .ns-trackcard, and deliberately no
     connector line between them — upstream's note: "nothing here claims one
     earns the next." The ordered progression is the .ns-path band above; this
     one is a menu.

     ⚠ NO HTML ENTITIES INSIDE the `t` helper. The helper escapes what it outputs, so
     "&amp;" written in the source is escaped a second time and renders on the
     page as the literal text "&amp;". Write the word, or a real "&" character
     — never the entity. This shipped once as "Security &amp; sharing".

     WHEN THESE BECOME REAL each card is a #training-module post and this file
     is deleted — training/modules already renders them. Do not grow a second
     module list here.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <header class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--between">
            <div>
                <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Sections"}}</span>
                <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Inside the stages"}}</h2>
                <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "The map of what the training covers. What is written so far is directly below."}}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ns-band__actions">
                <a class="ns-btn" href="#modules">{{t "See what is published"}}</a>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="ns-grid">
            <a class="ns-trackcard" href="#modules">
                <span class="ns-trackcard__head">
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__icon">{{> "icons/books"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__index">01</span>
                </span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__title">{{t "Platform foundations"}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__text">{{t "The org, the data model, and the words everything else is defined in."}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
            </a>

            <a class="ns-trackcard" href="#modules">
                <span class="ns-trackcard__head">
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__icon">{{> "icons/lock-simple"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__index">02</span>
                </span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__title">{{t "Security and sharing"}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__text">{{t "Who sees what, why, and what happens when a record is reparented."}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
            </a>

            <a class="ns-trackcard" href="#modules">
                <span class="ns-trackcard__head">
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__icon">{{> "icons/strategy"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__index">03</span>
                </span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__title">{{t "Automation with Flow"}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__text">{{t "Declarative first: records, screens, schedules, and the limits of each."}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
            </a>

            <a class="ns-trackcard" href="#modules">
                <span class="ns-trackcard__head">
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__icon">{{> "icons/code"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__index">04</span>
                </span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__title">{{t "Apex fundamentals"}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__text">{{t "Governor limits as a budget, bulkification as a habit, tests as proof."}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
            </a>

            <a class="ns-trackcard" href="#modules">
                <span class="ns-trackcard__head">
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__icon">{{> "icons/article"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__index">05</span>
                </span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__title">{{t "Reports and dashboards"}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__text">{{t "From a question to a chart someone else can trust, without exports."}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
            </a>

            <a class="ns-trackcard" href="#modules">
                <span class="ns-trackcard__head">
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__icon">{{> "icons/flask"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-trackcard__index">06</span>
                </span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__title">{{t "AI and Agentforce"}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__text">{{t "Prompt templates, grounding, actions — the platform's AI, demystified."}}</span>
                <span class="ns-trackcard__meta"><span>{{t "Planned"}}</span></span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
